From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps' notifications are ChromeOS
 notifications

Native Linux apps send notifications to org.freedesktop.Notifications and
Flatpak apps through the Notification portal; on NickelOS nothing showed
them. NickelOS's portal backend now serves both and asks Chrome for each:
vm_applications' NickelNotify(key, app_id, app_name, title, body, icon,
buttons, urgent) and NickelNotifyClose(key). NickelNotifications shows them
in the message center as Crostini's apps' notifications are shown
(CROSTINI_APPLICATION notifier, the Linux small icon), with the app's name,
its icon or the notification's image, and its buttons; an urgent one stays
until closed. Clicks go back through nickel-appd's NotificationEvent with
an xdg-activation token (exo's MakeActivationToken), so the app can bring
a window forward; so does the user's closing of it.

